# Architecture & Patterns

- Follow Clean Architecture principles: separate business logic from framework-specific code.
- Keep domain logic independent from UI framework details (Next.js/Expo concerns should not leak into core logic).
- Isolate side effects (network, storage, framework APIs) behind clear boundaries.

## Layering Guidance

- Domain/use-case code should depend on abstractions, not framework implementations.
- UI and route handlers should orchestrate data flow, not contain heavy business rules.
- Shared utilities should remain framework-agnostic when possible.

## Do

- Prefer dependency injection or thin adapters at boundaries.
- Keep modules cohesive with single, clear responsibilities.

## Don't

- Couple reusable business rules tightly to component lifecycle or router behavior.
